=== HYPOTHESIS ===
# p_7d2a — Standard split, v2: Marco's work kit leaves, journal at desk midday (fork of p_4a7c)

This fork of p_4a7c makes two corrections driven by the accumulating evidence. First, Marco's vitamins leave with him at 13:40. The per-object data shows vitamins_marco found at counter_k1 only 2 times in the 9–17 h window but absent 3 times; the two positive sightings almost certainly fall in the 9:00–13:40 sub-window when Marco is still home, while the three empty looks fall after 14:00 when he is at work. The p_b7c2 claim (vitamins OUT_OF_HOUSE 14–22 h) has earned 5 weak-for (empty looks at counter) against only 1 against, supporting the out-of-house reading. Second, the journal is at the bedroom desk during the midday window (11:00–14:00), not the nightstand. The p_e4c8 claim (desk at 11.5–13.5 h) has scored for 2, against 0, and the 12:00 sightings at desk_b1 (twice on the same day) are unambiguous. The journal returns to the nightstand by 14:00 and stays there overnight.

Everything else from p_4a7c is retained: lunchbox OUT_OF_HOUSE 13.5–23 h weekdays; Yuki's keys, jacket, sunglasses, water bottle at the entry during her walks; yoga mat on the living-room floor 06:00–06:45; guitar on the bedroom floor 15:00–16:30; standard meal and TV windows.

What sets this document apart from p_4a7c and p_8e2f: at 15:00 on a weekday, vitamins_marco is OUT_OF_HOUSE (not at counter_k1) and journal_marco is at desk_b1 (not at nightstand_b1). If the robot finds the vitamins at counter_k1 after 14:00 or the journal at the nightstand at 12:00, this document is refuted.

